  "_comment": "The person picker across the Mac bridge (docs/design-people.md § UX iteration 3). Vitest (frontend/src/utils/personPickerBridge.test.ts) builds each web_to_native `wire` from `input` with the English strings, and resolves each native_to_web `payload` against its `slot` to `effect`. Swift (BristlenoseTests/PersonPickerContractTests.swift) decodes every `wire` exactly as BridgeHandler receives it and builds every `payload` from `native`. Change a shape here first, then both sides. Version 3 (6 Oct 2026, design-people.md §J8): rows carry their own codes, the new row the next free one, and a reply says which row it came from — a listed name, a typed one (`new`) or That's Me (`me`) — so a typed name is never read as a pick. A reply the SPA refuses resolves to `{\"taken\": name}`.",
